# L3 — la TECNICA generalizza? Addestrabilita' che le ipotesi di L3 non
# prevedevano (§23). KB viva COMPLETA, NESSUN ritiro: i nomi qui sotto non sono
# collegati a niente, quindi ogni verde e' un vuoto vero che si riempie.
# Si lancia a mano; i tempi non sono un cancello (vedi banco.p0t).

[mock live]
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test e1 lessico di un'altra lingua, per contatto]
!timeout 0
> What is the Geburtsort of Napoleon?
< I don't know about geburtsort.
> Einstein was born in Ulm, so his Geburtsort is Ulm.
> What is the Geburtsort of Napoleon?
<~ ajaccio
> France borders Spain, so Spain is its Nachbar.
> What is the Nachbar of Italy?
<~ slovenia

[test e2 un altro consumatore lo usa senza essere toccato: la domanda polare]
!timeout 0
> Is Pisa the Geburtsort of Galileo Galilei?
<~ Yes

[test e3 dalla prosa, senza maestro: una frase di un paragrafo e' un contatto]
!timeout 0
> read: Marie Curie was born in Warsaw, so her Heimatstadt is Warsaw. She won two Nobel prizes.
> What is the Heimatstadt of Christopher Columbus?
<~ genoa

[test e4 un VERBO appreso per contatto e' un verbo di parrot0 (§24)]
!timeout 0
> Einstein was born in Ulm, so he hails from Ulm.
!query contact_shape(hails, born_in, $S)
> Where does Napoleon hail from?
<~ Reading «hail» as «was born in».
<~ Ajaccio

[test e5 la parola appresa LEGGE un'affermazione e scrive un fatto vero (§24)]
!timeout 0
> The Geburtsort of Kant is Konigsberg.
<~ Reading «geburtsort» as «was born in».
!query born_in(kant, konigsberg)
> Hegel hails from Stuttgart.
<~ Learned
!query born_in(hegel, stuttgart)

[test e6 e la domanda sul fatto appena letto usa la lingua di prima]
!timeout 0
> Where was Kant born?
<~ konigsberg
